# Local Herta canon corpus — large, derived/exported, not redistributable.
# The hybrid knowledge DB (.herta/knowledge/) is built from this; never commit either.
data/

# 板砖 (backend) scratch output during live testing — generated scripts,
# not part of the repo. `/scripts/*` (not `/scripts/`) so git still descends
# into the dir and the negation below can re-include a specific file (git
# cannot re-include a child of a wholly-excluded directory). Root-anchored
# so a package's own scripts/ dir (were one ever added) stays tracked.
# This public repo carries BUILD tools only — the dev archive keeps the
# live-lab and fixture scripts.
/scripts/*
# EXCEPT the prompt-asset codegen — a real build tool the Tier-1 prompt
# system depends on (edit packages/herta/prompts/**, rerun this, commit the
# regenerated prompt-assets.generated.ts). A fresh clone must have it.
!/scripts/generate-prompt-assets.mjs
!/scripts/bootstrap-windows.ps1
!/scripts/pnpm.ps1
!/scripts/verify-desktop.mjs
# AND the voice transcoder — wav masters → the shipped .opus clips (the
# 2026-07-16 opus cutover ships only what this regenerates).
!/scripts/transcode-voice.mjs

# Secrets — never commit
*-api-key.txt
*.pem
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Code-signing material (2026-08-06). A signing key committed to a public repo
# cannot be un-published — the remedy is revoking the certificate and burning
# one of the five Developer ID slots Apple allows. Generate this material
# outside the repo as well; this is the second line of defence, not the first.
*.p12
*.pfx
*.key
*.cer
*.crt
*.p8
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile
*.base64
*.keystore
*.jks
